<section class="ls-manifesto-chapter" id="standards">
<header class="ls-chapter-heading ls-container">
<p class="ls-eyebrow">04 / The standard</p>
<h2>SMALL ROUTINES. <span class="ls-stroke">BIGGER POSSIBILITIES.</span>
</h2>
</header>
<div class="ls-story-unit" data-tone="yellow">
<div class="ls-container">
<div class="ls-principle-pair">
<article class="ls-principle" data-principle="true" id="available-mac">
<span class="ls-principle-index">13 /</span>
<h3>FIND YOUR QUIET HOURS.</h3>
<p>Give recurring work a place in the day. Flow’s background helper can run with the app quit, while your Mac is plugged in and idle. Choose a nightly window. Return to a Morning Briefing that helps you begin.</p>
</article>
<article class="ls-principle" data-principle="true" id="better-model">
<span class="ls-principle-index">14 /</span>
<h3>KEEP THE METHOD AS INTELLIGENCE GROWS.</h3>
<p>Better models can widen what you attempt. Clear assignments, useful sources and thoughtful review give that capability somewhere to go. Keep the method visible, so each improvement can strengthen a practice you understand.</p>
</article>
</div>
